---

<IndividualPageLayout
    title={seoTitle}
    description={seoDescription}
    schema={pageSchema}
    pageTitle={pageTitle}
    heroImage="/media/titanium-aerospace-jet-engine-testing-hero.webp"
    heroImageAlt="Titanium aerospace jet engine undergoing a high-performance ground test with active exhaust"
    faqSectionTitle="Frequently Asked Questions: Open Die Forging"
    faqItems={faqs}
    ctaTitle="Request Quote For Open Die Forging"
    ctaDescription=""
    sourcesTitle="Sources"
    sourcesList={sources}
    resourcesTitle="Our Internal Resources for Die Casting, Investment casting, Forging and Sand Casting"
    resourcesList={internalResources}
>

    <div slot="full-width" class="individual-content">

        <section id="overview" >
            <div class="content-container">
                
                <h2>Open Die Forging: Extreme Strength for Massive Components</h2>

                <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center mt-6">
                    <div>
                        <p>
                            ForceBeyond provides world-class <a href="/open-die-forging" class="highlight-link">open die forging</a> (also known as free forging or smith forging) for massive, high-stress industrial applications. 
                            As part of our comprehensive <a href="/forging" class="highlight-link">custom forging services hub</a>, 
                            we shape heated metal between flat or contoured dies that do not completely enclose the material, producing extremely heavy components with unparalleled structural integrity.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Because open die forging does not require part-specific tooling, it is the most cost-effective method for low-volume runs, rapid prototyping, and parts too large for <a href="/closed-die-forging" class="highlight-link">closed die forging</a> presses. We supply heavy forged blocks, step shafts, discs, and rings using a broad range of alloys, including high-performance <a href="/superalloy-forging-services" class="highlight-link">exotic superalloys</a> like <a href="/inconel-718-supply" class="highlight-link">Inconel 718 forging</a> and specialized <a href="/eco-brass-c69300-forging" class="highlight-link">ECO BRASS C69300 forging</a>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="relative">
                        <div class="overflow-hidden">
                            <img
                                src="/media/precision-machined-stainless-steel-four-bolt-flange.webp"
                                alt="Precision-machined stainless steel four-bolt flange with a large central bore on a white background."
                                class="w-full h-auto object-cover hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500"
                            />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="technical-capabilities" >
            <div class="content-container">
                <h2>Technical Capabilities: Open Die Forged Shapes</h2>
                    <p>
                        Our <a href="/open-die-forging" class="highlight-link">open die forging capability</a> relies on the skill of press operators to incrementally shape the metal, which is subsequently precision-machined to final print tolerances. ForceBeyond manages massive weight capacities to manufacture diverse geometries:
                    </p>
                    <div class="content-table-wrapper">
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="col">Forged Geometry</th>
                                <th scope="col">Typical Applications & Related Technologies</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>

                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Step Shafts & Spindles</th>
                                <td>Power generation rotors, marine propeller shafts, and heavy industrial drive shafts.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Discs & Hubs</th>
                                <td>Gear blanks, heavy-duty machinery hubs, and high-pressure pipe flanges. For high-volume precision alternatives, compare with our <a href="/closed-die-forging" class="highlight-link">closed die forging</a> process.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Blocks & Rectangles</th>
                                <td>Tool steel blanks, massive structural supports, and heavy equipment bases engineered from structural alloys or <a href="/superalloy-forging-services" class="highlight-link">nickel-based superalloys</a>.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Cylinders & Sleeves</th>
                                <td>High-pressure containment vessels, hydraulic cylinders, and extrusion press components.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">Rings (Mandrel Forged)</th>
                                <td>Pressure vessel connections and heavy bearing races (for seamless high-production ring options, see our dedicated <a href="/rolled-ring-forging" class="highlight-link">Rolled Ring Forging</a> capabilities).</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="why-forcebeyond" >
            <div class="content-container">
                <h2>Why Partner with ForceBeyond for Open Die Forging?</h2>
                
                <p>
                    When components operate under critical stress, internal structural defects can result in catastrophic failure. Compared to traditional casting processes like <a href="/sand-casting" class="highlight-link">sand casting</a>, <a href="/investment-casting" class="highlight-link">investment casting</a>, or <a href="/die-casting" class="highlight-link">die casting</a>, open die forging delivers superior metallurgical density and strength.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Massive Size Capabilities:</strong> Open die forging is unbounded by mold cavity sizes. We forge components weighing from dozens of pounds up to 50,000+ lbs, with lengths extending dozens of feet.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Maximum Structural Integrity:</strong> Continuous hammering or pressing breaks down cast ingot structures, consolidating internal micro-shrinkage and refining grain structure for isotropic strength across heavy cross-sections.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Zero Custom Tooling Costs:</strong> Utilizing standard flat or V-shaped dies eliminates expensive custom die-sinking costs required in methods like <a href="/closed-die-forging" class="highlight-link">closed die forging</a> or <a href="/cold-forging" class="highlight-link">cold forging</a>.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Rapid Lead Times For Low Volumes:</strong> Without waiting for custom dies, open die forging allows fast lead times for prototypes, critical spares, and low-volume industrial runs.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="Tier-1.5-integration">
            <div class="content-container">
                <h2>Tier-1.5 Integration: Heavy Machining & Finishing</h2>
                <p>
                    Because open die forgings yield near-shape preforms, ForceBeyond seamlessly transitions your components from the forge shop to complete post-processing finishing across our <a href="/forging" class="highlight-link">global forging network</a>.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Heavy CNC Machining:</strong> Large-envelope vertical/horizontal lathes, boring mills, and heavy 5-axis centers deliver exact final dimensions to your print specifications.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Deep Hole Drilling:</strong> Precision internal boring for long step shafts, hollow cylinders, and high-pressure sleeves.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Advanced Heat Treatment:</strong> Deep-penetration normalizing, quenching, and tempering to achieve specific mechanical and tensile properties throughout massive sections.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Rigorous NDT & Inspection:</strong> Comprehensive Ultrasonic Testing (UT) to guarantee zero internal voids, supported by full Material Test Reports (MTRs) and ISO/AS9100 traceability.
                    </li>
                </ul>   
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="certified-applications" >
            <div class="content-container">
                <h2>Certified Open Die Forging Applications</h2>
                
                <p>
                    ForceBeyond delivers high-integrity open die forgings engineered for demanding operating environments:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Power Generation:</strong> Turbine shafts, generator rotors, and nuclear pressure boundary components.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Oil & Gas:</strong> Blowout preventers (BOPs), drilling collars, and subsea manifold blocks forged with corrosion-resistant alloys like <a href="/inconel-718-supply" class="highlight-link">Inconel 718</a> or <a href="/duplex-stainless-steel-casting" class="highlight-link">Duplex Stainless Steel</a>.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Mining & Heavy Equipment:</strong> Excavator main shafts, rock crusher hubs, and large gear blanks.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Shipbuilding & Marine:</strong> Propeller shafts, rudder stocks, and structural submarine components.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>
        
    </div>
</IndividualPageLayout>